  "item_one_liners": {},
  "label": "Ai Driven Molecular Binder Design",
  "related": [
    "untitled-topic-03cd",
    "untitled-topic-b7b3",
    "microbiome-rhizosphere-34b7"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "plasma-alzheimer-0312",
  "summary": "Wet-lab closed loops and free-energy ranking are now coupling generative models to experimental validation of binders and inhibitors.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is computational design of functional molecules coupled to experimental testing. Agentic LLM workflows ran three wet-lab design-test-improve cycles to generate aptamers against α-thrombin and myoglobin. A prospective study combined fragment-based generative design with alchemical absolute binding free-energy ranking to yield nanomolar LasB inhibitors. A negative result reports 627 BindCraft2 trajectories yielding zero accepted binders against the LDHA K81 lactylation epitope, documenting a failure mode of such pipelines. Multimodal generative learning targets the tight coupling among RNA sequence, structure, and function, while a review surveys AlphaFold 3 and RoseTTAFoldNA across the aptamer pipeline. Predictive ADME and potency models for coronavirus main protease inhibitors and explainable graph prioritization of antimicrobial natural products extend the same logic to small-molecule screening.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-18"
}
